that makes some kind of product and you have your employees at that company who are buying products from a rival, in some ways it tells you that the people who are presumably your most loyal, who should be your most loyal customers are in fact not your loyal customers and that should raise red flags about customers in general. Well, what it tells you is there's, I'll use the language of Clay Christensen and Tony Ulwick here, there's a job to be done

